# Push finished work to GitHub

This is Project H.O.R (`vacancy`). Its GitHub remote is
https://github.com/Gan-Jax/vacancy

After you change project files, publish those changes. Do not wait to be asked.

## When to push

- After finishing a feature, fix, or other file change
- Treat a completed task as permission to commit and push
- If Project RM (`hotel-simulator`) also changed, update that repo separately

## How

1. Review `git status` and `git diff`
2. Do not commit secrets (`.env`, credentials, keys)
3. Do not commit Unity generated folders (`Library/`, `Temp/`, `Obj/`, `Logs/`)
4. Commit with a short message that explains why
5. `git push` to `origin` on the current branch
6. Mention the GitHub URL when done

## Do not

- Leave finished work only on this machine
- Skip the push because the user did not say "commit" or "push"
- Change git config, force-push, or skip hooks
